    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "p2p: replace full outbound peers that don't support tx relay (take 2)",
    "user": {
      "login": "fjahr",
      "id": 1322187,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjIxODc=",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1322187?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/fjahr",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/fjahr",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fjahr/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fjahr/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fjahr/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fjahr/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fjahr/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fjahr/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fjahr/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fjahr/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fjahr/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "Picks up #28538\r\n\r\nOutbound-full-relay slots should be used by peers that actually relay transactions, besides #28538 see #16418 and #28371 for the motivation. So try to replace peers that are not relaying txs with peers that do.\r\n\r\nThe approach differs from the original PR in a few details in response to some of the review comments there:\r\n\r\n- A replacement is connected before the peer is evicted. The original PR disconnected a non-tx-relaying peer once all full outbound slots were filled. Reviewers preferred having a replacement available first (https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/28538#issuecomment-1883481846). Now an extra outbound-full-relay connection is requested, like the extra network-specific peers, and the existing eviction of extra outbound peers prefers peers that don't relay txs.\r\n- Peers not relaying txs don't get `m_protect`. Otherwise they could stay forever (https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/28538#discussion_r1443336121), and ignoring the protection was rejected in the same thread (https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/28538#discussion_r1443312604).\r\n- An only peer on a network is not replaced. Otherwise the network-specific extra connections and this logic would keep replacing each other (https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/28538#issuecomment-1883481846). This also covers the `-maxconnections=1` case (https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/28538#discussion_r1417178196).\r\n\r\nNothing is changed in `-blocksonly` mode or during IBD. The rename commit and the functional test are taken from the original PR with some changes to match the new behavior.",
